|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.90 | 0% | 79% | 0.529 | never | never | never |
| 0.90 | 20% | 63% | 0.730 | never | never | never |
| 0.90 | 40% | 47% | 0.810 | never | never | never |
| 0.90 | 60% | 32% | 0.854 | over 4000 | over 4000 | over 4000 |
| 0.90 | 80% | 16% | 0.881 | 410 | 487 | 487 / 97 / 24 |
| 0.90 | 100% | 0% | 0.900 | 150 | 150 | 150 / 30 / 7.5 |
| 0.95 | 0% | 83% | 0.704 | never | never | never |
| 0.95 | 20% | 66% | 0.851 | over 4000 | over 4000 | over 4000 |
| 0.95 | 40% | 50% | 0.900 | 150 | 299 | 299 / 60 / 15 |
| 0.95 | 60% | 33% | 0.925 | 76 | 114 | 114 / 23 / 5.7 |
| 0.95 | 80% | 17% | 0.940 | 50 | 60 | 60 / 12 / 3.0 |
| 0.95 | 100% | 0% | 0.950 | 40 | 40 | 40 / 8.0 / 2.0 |
| 0.98 | 0% | 86% | 0.860 | 3790 | 26596 | 26596 / 5319 / 1330 |
| 0.98 | 20% | 69% | 0.936 | 59 | 188 | 188 / 38 / 9.4 |
| 0.98 | 40% | 51% | 0.959 | 40 | 82 | 82 / 16 / 4.1 |
| 0.98 | 60% | 34% | 0.970 | 30 | 46 | 46 / 9.1 / 2.3 |
| 0.98 | 80% | 17% | 0.976 | 30 | 36 | 36 / 7.2 / 1.8 |
| 0.98 | 100% | 0% | 0.980 | 30 | 30 | 30 / 6.0 / 1.5 |
CE G1-bias: at a true agreement of 0.90 the measured agreement passes 0.85 only while at least 58% of accepts are examined (a glanced share of at most 33%): below the fatigue line of 40%, so the gate closes before the fatigue rule acts
note at a true agreement of 0.95 the measured agreement passes 0.85 only while at least 20% of accepts are examined (a glanced share of at most 66%)
note at a true agreement of 0.98 the measured agreement passes 0.85 only while at least 0% of accepts are examined (a glanced share of at most 86%)
CE G1-pick: before the hold tier nothing is "escalated", so no denominator binds: an Overlord right on 70% of rows that seals predictions only on the 50% it is surest of (right on 95% of those) shows 0.95 and passes the first gate at 40 cases
note the same Overlord scored on blind answers alone passes at 150, 40, 30 cases (p 0.90, 0.95, 0.98): 1200, 320, 240 operator answers

## T3. The third gate: a change of model, skill or card template (Table 9.5a)
| replay set | bound at n of n | one answer changed | two changed | three changed | changed answers the gate tolerates |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 19 | 0.854 | -0.069 | -0.133 | -0.193 | 0 |
CE G3-noise: a replay set of 19: one changed answer moves the bound by 0.069, more than the gate's 0.05
| 30 | 0.905 | -0.043 | -0.084 | -0.124 | 1 |
| 40 | 0.928 | -0.033 | -0.065 | -0.096 | 1 |
| 60 | 0.951 | -0.022 | -0.043 | -0.064 | 2 |
| 100 | 0.970 | -0.013 | -0.025 | -0.037 | 4 |
| 200 | 0.985 | -0.006 | -0.012 | -0.018 | 8 |
| 400 | 0.993 | -0.003 | -0.006 | -0.009 | 17 |
| replay set | false failure at equal true agreement 0.90 | at 0.95 |
|---|---|---|
| 30 | 26% | 25% |
CE G3-noise: a replay set of 30 and no change in judgement: the gate fails 25% of changes (independent replays, true agreement 0.95)
| 60 | 22% | 15% |
CE G3-noise: a replay set of 60 and no change in judgement: the gate fails 15% of changes (independent replays, true agreement 0.95)
| 100 | 15% | 12% |
CE G3-noise: a replay set of 100 and no change in judgement: the gate fails 12% of changes (independent replays, true agreement 0.95)
| 200 | 8% | 3% |
| 400 | 2% | 0% |
CE G3-ratchet: each change passes at "the last generation's less 0.05": a kind armed at 0.90 answers at 0.85, 0.80, 0.75, 0.70, 0.65, 0.60 after 6 changes, every gate green
note Table 9.5a gives the third gate no least count: before the first gate passes, the replay set is under 30 cases

