note before a cell acts, a weekly spot-check has nothing to draw from it: its only source is the blind sample of its escalations
note once a cell acts, its rows are answered and no longer escalated: the blind sample stops, and the record grows by at most 3 spot-checks a week, shared by every cell
note a cell that needs 59 clean cases and gets only spot-checks: 20 weeks if every spot-check of every week fell in it

## T5. The grant gate (§7.2, Table 9.5a)
note 19 blind cases pass only at 19 of 19; one miss needs 30 blind cases, two need 40
reading: evidence per effect and scope, a cap under 19 -> unsatisfiable: every case is from the scope's one programme
reading: evidence per effect and scope, a cap 19 or more -> the cap never binds
reading: evidence per effect, across programmes, a cap under 19 -> satisfiable, and §7.2's "one scope" is false
CE G2-cap: a scope is one programme: "a cap on cases from one programme" is either unsatisfiable (a cap under 19) or never binds
note 19 blind cases at one in eight are 152 questions of one effect in one programme: 152 / 30 / 7.6 days at 1 / 5 / 20 such questions a day
note with one miss: 240 questions; the five days are met by then at any rate under 30 a day
CE G2-window: the grant evidence has "the window" and no length for it: at 30 days the gate needs 5.1 questions a day of one effect in one programme, at 90 days 1.7, at 180 days 0.8
note a renewal needs three acts under the grant in its 30 days; an O3 item of one effect in one programme may come less often

## T6. The label queue (§3.7)
ok  a 10% target needs 29 clean answers and a 5% target 59
note 12 rows take their labels from the queue; their lines need 378 labels beyond the line in all: 38 weeks at ten a week, if every card lands beyond a line
| how the ten cards are shared | first line admitted | `scope.widens` (a gate, 59) | last line admitted | rows with no line after 400 weeks |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| oldest case first | week 11 | week 26 | week 152 | 0 |
| newest case first | week 5 | week - | - | 5 |
CE LQ-starve: ten cards a week shared "newest case first": 5 rows never reach a line (scope.widens ...)
| equal shares | week 13 | week 27 | week 39 | 0 |
| a gate first, then the row nearest its line | week 6 | week 6 | week 38 | 0 |
CE LQ-source: `grant.inside` needs 59 labelled yes answers with no error, and its one label source, `overturn`, labels a yes only as wrong: its line is never admitted

